# systemd user unit for the daily agent-bridge memory hygiene pass.
#
# Runs the full hygiene cycle back-to-back in a single oneshot (ζ-10).
# Order is deliberate: clean before stamp before reward, snapshot last.
#
#   1. `dream decay-unused`   — Phase 2.x #8: shave `importance` on memory
#                               rows whose last_accessed_at is older than
#                               --window-days. Pairs with Palace C7/C8/C10
#                               stale UI so retrieval rank tracks viewer.
#   2. `dream prune-coactivation-noise` — δ-3 (Butlin HOT-4): drop coact
#                               pairs that fired once briefly and never
#                               grew again (count <= --max-count AND
#                               last_at older than --older-than-days).
#                               Pairs with dream promote — anything still
#                               below the promote threshold after the
#                               window is by definition synaptic noise.
#   3. `dream prune-degenerate-relates` — ζ-12: delete `relates` edges
#                               whose BOTH endpoints carry a blacklist
#                               tag. Cleans the legacy noise hubs that
#                               pre-ζ-11 `memory_link_orphans` runs
#                               collapsed auto_curated stubs onto. Pairs
#                               with `memory_link_orphans skip_tags` (ζ-11
#                               preventive layer — applied by MCP tool,
#                               not in cron).
#   4. `dream archive-orphan-stubs` — ζ-14: flip orphan stubs whose tags
#                               overlap the blacklist from active to
#                               archived once they have aged past
#                               --older-than-days. Closes the ζ-9→ζ-12
#                               loop by retiring signal-poor stubs that
#                               ζ-11 would never re-link. ζ-15: with
#                               --alarm-threshold N, archives >= N
#                               also save a `kind=alert` memory + log
#                               to stderr so the journal flags bursts.
#   5. `dream promote`        — Hebbian wire-together (tier 1):
#                               crystallise co-fire pairs with count >=
#                               --min-count (default 5, weight 0.5-0.95)
#                               into explicit `cofires` edges. Skips
#                               pairs that already have a `cofires` edge
#                               (idempotent).
#   6. `dream promote --tier 2` — Secondary promotion (P16-M):
#                               crystallise recurring-but-weak pairs
#                               (count >= 3) that have NO existing edge
#                               of any type into `co_referenced` edges
#                               (weight 0.3-0.5). Salvages the mid-tier
#                               signal that tier 1 misses. Skips on ANY
#                               existing edge so it doesn't pollute
#                               structural connections.
#   7. `dream reinforce-active` — Hebbian wire-strengthen: bump
#                               `importance` by --step (capped at
#                               --ceiling) for every row with
#                               access_count >= --min-access AND
#                               last_accessed_at within --window-days.
#                               Positive-reinforcement mirror of #1 —
#                               without it, the system is entropy-monotonic
#                               (decay only, never reward).
#   8. `dream tombstone-aged-archived` — ζ-19: time-based downgrade of
#                               stale archived → tombstoned. Default
#                               14-day window leaves a generous ζ-18
#                               restore opportunity. Bridges ζ-14
#                               (archive) to the existing 7d
#                               purge-tombstones cycle so the retire
#                               state machine eventually reaches DELETE.
#   9. `dream purge-tombstones` — Phase 2.x #6: hard-DELETE rows that
#                               have been tombstoned for at least
#                               --older-than-days. Tombstone soft-delete
#                               keeps deleted rows for `agent-bridge sync`
#                               to propagate; this collects them once
#                               past the sync window. Runs BEFORE
#                               snapshot so the snapshot reflects the
#                               post-GC state.
#  10. `dream snapshot`       — ζ-1 + ζ-9 v2: dump a daily self-portrait
#                               (memory counts, coactivation, attention,
#                               identity, transitions, topology) as a
#                               `snapshot_daily_YYYYMMDD_HHMM` memory.
#                               Goes last so the snapshot reflects the
#                               post-hygiene state — tomorrow's `dream
#                               diff <today> <yesterday>` then surfaces
#                               the net daily delta.
#
# All ops are pure SQL, no LLM, idempotent. `ExecStart=-` lets each run
# even if a sibling fails; failure modes are unlikely (no network, no
# LLM, no auth).
#
# Filename keeps `memory-decay-unused` for backward compat with the
# initial install (Mac + aio2 already enabled). Migration is just
# `git pull && ./scripts/systemd/install.sh`.
#
# Install (see also `install.sh` next to this file):
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
#   cp scripts/systemd/agent-bridge-memory-decay-unused.service ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   cp scripts/systemd/agent-bridge-memory-decay-unused.timer   ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user enable --now agent-bridge-memory-decay-unused.timer
#
# One-shot manual run (don't wait for timer):
#   systemctl --user start agent-bridge-memory-decay-unused.service
#
# Logs (both ops append to the same file):
#   tail -f ~/.cache/agent-bridge/memory-decay-unused.log
#
# Tuning: override either ExecStart via `systemctl --user edit` (drop-in).
# Reset the matching line to empty first, e.g.:
#   [Service]
#   ExecStart=
#   ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream decay-unused \
#       --window-days 14 --step 0.03 --floor 0.05

[Unit]
Description=agent-bridge daily memory hygiene (ζ-10 full cycle — decay + prune + archive[+ζ-15 alarm] + promote(T1+T2) + reinforce + tombstone-aged + purge-tombstones + snapshot)
Documentation=file://%h/.claude/projects/-Data-CascadeProjects-agent-bridge/memory/project_memory_decay_unused_cron_shipped.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# `.real` bypasses the wrapper's ANTHROPIC_* injection — every op below
# is pure SQL, no LLM, so wrapper env scaffolding is dead weight.
# `ExecStart=-` so a transient failure on one op doesn't block the others
# (e.g. lock contention with palace serve or dream replay).
#
# Order: subtract (decay → prune-coact → prune-relates → archive) → add
# (promote T1 → promote T2 → reinforce-active) → GC (tombstone-aged →
# purge-tombstones) → record (snapshot). Subtract first to remove dead
# weight, then build new attention structure from the cleaned coact
# data (promote tier 1 first so tier 2 can see the fresh cofires when
# applying its "skip any edge" rule), then strengthen importance, then
# walk the retire state machine forward (archived → tombstoned →
# DELETE), then capture the post-hygiene state so tomorrow's diff sees
# a clean delta.
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream decay-unused --window-days 30 --step 0.05 --floor 0.1
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream prune-coactivation-noise --max-count 1 --older-than-days 30
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream prune-degenerate-relates
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream archive-orphan-stubs --older-than-days 3 --alarm-threshold 25
# P20 — Hebbian wire-together. Tier 1 first (count >= 5, weight 0.5-0.95)
# then tier 2 (count >= 3, weight 0.3-0.5, skips any-edge pairs only).
# Order matters: tier-1 must run first so tier-2's "skip any existing
# edge" check sees today's freshly-promoted cofires and stays out of
# their way. Both write fresh edges to memory_edges so the post-hygiene
# snapshot in step 8 captures the day's attention-structure growth.
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream promote
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream promote --tier 2
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream reinforce-active --window-days 7 --min-access 5 --step 0.10 --ceiling 0.95
# ζ-19 — retire state machine step. Stale archived rows (updated_at
# 14+ days ago, set by ζ-14 at archive time) get downgraded to
# tombstoned. The 14d window comfortably outstrips ζ-18's restore
# horizon; tombstone (not direct DELETE) preserves the dedupe_key slot
# until the next step's 7-day purge cycle.
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream tombstone-aged-archived --older-than-days 14 --max-count 500
# P22 — sync-window GC for tombstones. older-than-days 7 matches the
# Mac/aio2 cross-machine sync cadence; tombstones live long enough for
# sync to propagate the soft-delete, then this collects them. Runs
# BEFORE snapshot so snapshot captures the post-GC active count.
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream purge-tombstones --older-than-days 7
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/agent-bridge.real dream snapshot --name daily
StandardOutput=append:%h/.cache/agent-bridge/memory-decay-unused.log
StandardError=append:%h/.cache/agent-bridge/memory-decay-unused.log
TimeoutStartSec=300
